  "findings": [
    "the container is limited to 57.7 GiB of memory while MemTotal reports 251.5 GiB, a 4.4x overstatement Stage 1.1 did not observe. Capacity from MemTotal would have authorized four times what exists and the workloads would have been OOM-killed. The RAM version of the four visible accelerators where one was assigned",
    "filesystem credibility had to be an allow-list, not a deny-list: the first version trusted any family it did not recognise as networked, which fails open on exactly the surprising mount that matters. Caught by a test written for a made-up filesystem type"
